From: Redmi 9 mainline port <lancelot@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] iio: adc: mt6359-auxadc: Mask out the data ready bit of the IMP channel

mt6358_read_imp() hands the raw content of the AUXADC_ADC28 register
back to the IIO core. Bit 15 of that register is the ADC data ready
flag (AUXADC_ADC_RDY_IMP), not part of the conversion result, and it
is still set when the value is read.

As a consequence the reported raw value can exceed the 15 bit channel
resolution, e.g. 0xdca8 instead of 0x5ca8, making the computed voltage
almost three times too high.

The MediaTek vendor code masks the register with 0x7fff
(PMIC_AUXADC_ADC_OUT_IMP_MASK) before using it; do the same, using the
channel resolution just like mt6359_auxadc_read_adc() already does.
---
 drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c

--- a/drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c
@@ -501,8 +501,13 @@
 
 	mt6358_stop_imp_conv(adc_dev);
 
+	/*
+	 * Bit 15 of the ADC output register is the data ready flag, which is
+	 * still set at this point: mask it out, otherwise the returned raw
+	 * value overflows the channel resolution.
+	 */
 	if (vbat)
-		*vbat = val_v;
+		*vbat = val_v & GENMASK(chan->scan_type.realbits - 1, 0);
 	if (ibat)
 		*ibat = 0;
 
